    25	#      the extremes on shared diagonals and accidentally mix intended pairs.
    26	#      new logic: identify A and C as red-marked, B and D as green-marked, then connect
    27	#      only A↔C and B↔D; triggers are read only along those chosen diagonals.
    28	#
    29	# b) Complexity calibration:
    30	#    - To make the new rule visually inferable, each generated grid has at least two
    31	#      marker colors, and every marker color appears exactly twice.
